  "recipe": {
    "technique": "Bacini were used in quantity, buildings with just one or two installed are rare. Some churches in Pisa (San Piero a Grado, San Martino, Santa Cecilia) had over 200 bacini each. The location of bacini in the building varied, but typically they were placed high up: at the clerestory level, in the blind arcades, on the sides of bell towers. Occasionally, the bowls on the facades were arranged into a figure of cross. Five-bacini crosses were popular in Crete, and are quite rare in mainland Greece and Italy."
  },
